# ── Interpretation (honest scope — do not widen) ──
# What this proves: terem-core's resolve → license-gate → launch-plan → spawn →
# serial/QMP plumbing works against a REAL operator-installed QEMU on this host,
# and the hand-assembled in-repo 512-byte boot sector is genuinely bootable:
# SeaBIOS loaded the El Torito no-emulation image at 0x7C00 and executed it to
# the TEREM-LIVE-QEMU-MARKER-V1 serial marker under an operator-supplied QEMU.
# What this does NOT prove: no OS booted (the fixture is 512 bytes of real-mode
# polling code, not a guest); no isolation, TEE, attestation, or security
# property of any kind is claimed or tested; QEMU's own correctness/safety is
# out of scope (it is the operator's external GPL-2.0 process, never ours);
# everything remains UNAUDITED. A real guest-OS boot is a different, later
# proof requiring a real guest image — deliberately unclaimed here.
